|----------E100.FFFF
Contact with the programmer is broken
      PROMlink is no longer in communication with the programmer.
      Possible reasons for this are:

      1)  The cable connecting the programmer to the computer has pulled
          loose.

      2)  The programmer is no longer turned on or the programmer is no
          longer in computer remote control mode.

      3)  The baud rate are set differently on the programmer and in the
          configuration file.  The default baud rate is 9600.   

      4)  The programmer is not connected to the port specified in the
          configuration file.  The default port is COM1.  

|----------E101.FFFF
Cannot open user file
      The requested file could not be opened by PROMlink.  Possible
      reasons are:

      1)  The file name was mis-typed; try the operation again with
          the correct file name.

      2)  The file requested was not on the specified disk.  Put the
          correct disk in the drive or specify the correct drive.

      3)  The disk was not in the drive or the drive door was not closed.
          Put the disk in the drive and try the operation again.
|----------E102.FFFF
Unable to rename file
      The specified file can not be renamed by PROMlink. Possible reasons are:

      1)  The file to be renamed is not found.

      2)  The new file name already exists.

      3)  The new file name is not specified.

      4)  The drive is empty.  Put the disk in the drive and try the operation
          again.
|----------E103.FFFF
Cannot write to file
      PROMlink cannot continue to write to the specified file.  Possible
      reasons for this are:

      1)  The disk has no free space left.  A different disk must be
          used or some files must be erased from this one to leave
          enough room for the new information.

      2)  The disk is write protected.  A different disk must be used
          or the write-protect tab removed from this one.

      3)  The drive is empty.  Put the disk in the drive and try the
          operation again.
|----------E104.FFFF
PROMlink I/O buffer overflow.
      The programmer ignored the software handshake.

      Try the operation again.
|----------E105.FFFF
-
Cannot write configuration file to the current directory.
