|----------E121.FFFF
Unknown command has been sent to the programmer
      The programmer does not understand the CRC command sent by PROMlink.
      Possible reason are: 
 
      1)  You are trying to use the Begin Handler Programming function 
          while your Programmer/Pak does not have the Handler option.

      2)  You attempted to set Setsize or Bit Mode and your Programmer/Pak
          is neither a Model 121 nor a GangPak.

      3)  The Programmer/Pak you are using is not the same as what
          you have specified.

      4)  If you got this error while PROMlink was executing User Functions,
          this means that your User Function file contains a CRC command
          unknown to the Programmer/Pak.  Check your User Function file
          carefully.
|----------E122.FFFF
Unable to change drive
      PROMlink can not change the default drive to the requested drive.
      Possible reasons are:

      1) The specified drive is empty.  Put the disk in the drive and try
         the operation again.

      2) Invalid drive specifier
|----------E123.FFFF
Unable to display directory
      The requested directory can not be displayed. Possible reasons are:

      1)  No such directory.

      2)  Specified file not found.

      3)  No disk in the drive.  Put the disk in the drive and try the
          operation again.
|----------E124.FFFF
Unable to change directory
      PROMlink can not change the current directory to the requested
      directory.  Possible reasons are:

      1)  No such directory.

      2)  No disk in the drive.  Put the disk in the drive and try the
          operation again.
|----------E125.FFFF
Illegal user function file
      Your user function file has a bad format.  Possible reasons are:

      1)  The first 2 charters of your file are not a backslash followed
          by a double quote (\"), which should mark the beginning of the
	  first menu item name.

      2)  There is a double quote (") in the file which is not preceded by
          a backslash (\) to mark the beginning of a menu item name, nor is
          it the closing mark of a \%M User Function command.

      3)  There is a backslash (\) in the file which is not followed by a
          percent character (%) in defining a User Function command.
          All User Function command definitions must begin with backslash
          percent (\%).
|----------E126.FFFF
User function file too big
     Not enough memory to load the specified user function file.
|----------E127.FFFF
Too many menu items in user function file
     A user function file cannot have more than 10 menu items.
|----------E128.FFFF
Error on menu item line
     Illegal menu item in User Function file.  Possible reasons are:

     1)  It has more than 24 characters.

     2)  It does not start with a backslash followed by a double quote (\").

     3)  It does not end with a double quote (").

     4)  It contains a linefeed or a TAB.
|----------E129.FFFF
Unexpected end of user function file
     Your User Function ended after sending a CRC command to the programmer
     without issuing a User Function command to define the action to be
     taken afterwards.  
|----------E130.FFFF
Unknown User Function command
     There are a total of seven User Function commands:
        \%E
        \%>
        \%*
        \%P
        \%D
        \%R
        \%M
     A User Function command which is not one of the commands listed above
     is found in your User Function file.
 
     For detailed information on User Function commands, refer to your
     PROMlink manual.
|----------E131.FFFF
Illegal binning signal
     Values of binning signals can only be in the range of 1-5.
|----------E132.FFFF
Illegal port number
-
|----------E133.FFFF
