     As binary data was received from the programmer during a 'Create file
     from RAM' operation, a sumcheck test indicated a data transmission error.

     Check all connections and try the operation again.
|----------E134.FFFF
Sumcheck error during binary file create
     As binary data was received from the programmer during a 'Create file
     from RAM' operation, a data header format test indicated a data
     transmission error.

     Check all connections and try again.
|----------E135.FFFF
Sumcheck error during binary file create
     As binary data was received from the programmer during a 'Create file
     from RAM' operation, a data trailer format test indicated a data
     transmission error.

     Check all connections and try the operation again.
|----------E136.FFFF
Binary format cannot be used with current Parity and Data Bits
     Binary format cannot be used for two possible reasons:

     1)  Parity is set to odd or even.

     2)  Number of Data Bits is set to 7.

     If you want to use Binary format in 'Load RAM from file' or
     'Create file from RAM', change Parity to 'no parity' and set
     the number of data bits to 8.
|----------E137.FFFF
Unable to delete file(s)
     PROMlink cannot delete specified file(s).  Possible reasons are:

     1)  File(s) not found.

     2)  File(s) have been marked read-only.
|----------E138.FFFF
Undefined User Function
     The User Function you selected from the User Function menu is an
